r><br><b>Although rates vary, here is a representative example of how APRs and fees are calculated:</b><br><br>A loan of $1,000 taken out for one year with a 17% APR will cost you:<br>\u2022 Total charge for loan: $1,000 * 0.17 (17% APR) = $170<br>\u2022 Total amount you repay: $1,000 + $170 = $1,170<br>\u2022 Monthly payment: $1,170 / 12 months = $97.5",
